@* Accounting tab "Wallet Configuration" link → FDBGrid "Book of Accounts" editor as a modal
   (VB6 lblEditList_Click Index 11 → FDBGrid.ShowForm("Book of Accounts", …, "DataSources",
   "BookOfAccount", False, , "WalletPartyID")). FDBGrid's caption resolver builds the exact
   VB6 SQL (incl. the Sage300/Timberline conditional columns + the post-close DataSourceID
   GUID backfill), so we drive it by FormCaption alone. *@
@if (_showBookOfAccountsModal)
{
    <FDBGrid IsModal="true" OnClose="OnBookOfAccountsClosed" FormCaption="Book of Accounts" />
}

@* Conditional-Formatting tab "Tax groups..." link → FDBGrid "Tax Groups" editor as a modal
   (VB6 lblEditList_Click Index 2 → FDBGrid.ShowForm("Tax Groups", s, "taxgroups",
   "divisionid,taxgroup", <ReadOnly if Timberline>, "divisionid")). VB6 passes "divisionid"
   as the HIDDEN-columns arg (6th positional); the caption resolver instead treats it as a
   locked column, so to stay byte-faithful we drive this instance by an explicit ShowForm(…)
   call (one-shot in OnAfterRenderAsync) with hiddenColumns:"divisionid" and a parameterized
   DivisionID. *@
@if (_showTaxGroupsModal)
{
    <FDBGrid @ref="_taxGroupsGrid" IsModal="true" OnClose="OnTaxGroupsClosed" FormCaption="Tax Groups" />
}

